# Using Fetch in mounted()

```javascript
export default {
  data() {
    return {
      users: []
    }
  },
  async mounted() {
    const response = await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users')
    this.users = await response.json()
  }
}
```

This fetches data when the component is created and stores it in `users`. The template can then render the list.

⚠️ **Note**: `mounted` is the typical place for initial data fetching because the component is already in the DOM.
